<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Reggies lifts half-yr shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Reggies lifts half-yr shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     3.96     vs   1.93</p>
<p>    Net income		2.98     vs   1.32</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   4.45     vs   2.04</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.47     vs   0.72</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.78     vs   0.13</p>
<p>    Turnover		127.26     vs  61.12</p>
<p>Full name: Redgwoods Holdings Ltd (retail)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that while high interest rates and poor exchange rates had affected trading, directors were cautiously optimistic that the good trend in profit growth for the interim would continue for the rest of the year, though not at the same rate.</p>
<p>The company recently announced a 10.5 million rand rights issue, the proceeds of which would be used to fund expansion.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
